      "point": "The ticking sound in the score is built from a recording of Nolan's own pocket watch, and the music uses a Shepard tone, an illusion of endlessly rising pitch, which the script was written to fit. He had used the same device in The Prestige.",
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunkirk_(2017_film)"
    },
    {
      "point": "The Germans are never shown on screen and Churchill and the war rooms are left out on purpose, so viewers only know what the men on the ground could know.",
